mail-submit sends a single mail message using SMTP over TLS

Usage: mail-submit [to...] <mail

The arguments are the list of envelope recipients.

After reading its config, mail-submit reads an RFCxxx mail message on
stdin, adds Date and Message-ID header fields, and sends the message
to its configured server.

It uses SASL PLAIN for authentication and blocks until the server
confirms receipt of the message.
